# Baarik — environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Values are deliberately absent from this file:
# it is committed, and a template with a working key in it is how keys leak.
#
# Everything here is read once, at boot, by src/server/config/env.ts. A missing or
# malformed variable stops the process immediately rather than surfacing later as a
# 500 on whichever request happened to touch that code path first.

# --- Gemini credentials -----------------------------------------------------------
#
# At least one key is required; the app refuses to start without one.
#
# Free-tier quota is enforced per key and the ceilings are unpublished, so more than
# one key is strongly recommended. The server round-robins across them and moves a key
# to the back of the rotation as soon as it answers 429, which turns a rate limit into
# a slower response rather than an outage.
#
# Two shapes are accepted and may be mixed. Keys are de-duplicated, so a key appearing
# in both forms is held once.
#
#   1. One key, or several separated by commas or whitespace:
GEMINI_API_KEY=
#
#   2. Any number of suffixed variables. The suffix is not interpreted — the server
#      scans for the `GEMINI_API_KEY` prefix — so new ones can be added here without
#      changing any code.
# GEMINI_API_KEY2=
# GEMINI_API_KEY3=
#
# No format check is applied to a key. Google's key format has already changed once,
# and only the network can tell you whether a key is live; a dead key is demoted by
# the rotation rather than rejected at startup.

# --- Runtime ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `development`, `test` or `production`. Next.js normally sets this; declare it only
# when running the server outside the Next.js CLI. Defaults to `development`.
# NODE_ENV=

# `trace`, `debug`, `info`, `warn`, `error` or `fatal`. Defaults to `info`.
#
# No level ever causes document text, quotes or extracted facts to be logged. That is
# a property of what the code passes to the logger, not of this setting.
# LOG_LEVEL=
